Hello, I'm playing Nethack for about two years now and I have a few
suggestion that might be interested on the next versions:

- Kick monsters away
This would be a good use for the very underated kick in battle, you
could kick a monster of light/medium weight far from you to avoid him,
this would be particularly good when you're are running for your life
from cats or dogs, or for a ranger who is using a bow.
Who in real life never kicked a annoying cat far away?

- A "creature" character role
I assume that adding lot's of races to the current roles isn't a very
wise ideia. So I guess it would be interesting if you could add a new
role that not is really role, it allow you to choose unusual races to
play with (playing with goblins, nymps or trolls whould be fun). I
know you can do that with polymorph, but starting with those would be
a cool addition.

- Dark/Moon elves?
I belive the evil dark elves race is somewhat new from d&d, I think it
would be interested because we need elf rogues, playing dark elf
rogues would raise the perseption which would be nice.

- Half creatures
I doubt you guys never discussed something like this before, I wonder
if it is all that necessary, but just in case: It would be a good
addition having Half-Elves, Half-Orcs and Half-Dragons.

